From 2158889f3a959a060f9515c64bde2cec718b05ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 12:35:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign web UI: light Meet-style theme, real trend chart,
 hideable stats
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Force a single clean white/light theme (Meet-inspired) instead of the
  dark-only palette; add CSS tokens for surface/border/accent colors.
- Replace the "last 60s" sparkline, which only plotted the quantized
  argmax engagement level, with a real multi-line trend of the four
  live state probabilities (Bored/Confused/Engaged/Frustrated) with a
  matching color-coded legend, so the chart visibly reflects live model
  output instead of reading like a placeholder.
- Give each state its own color (bars, legend, trend) instead of a
  single uniform accent, for faster at-a-glance reading.
- Restructure CognitiveApp into a Meet-style layout: compact header
  with a pulsing "Live" badge + session timer, video tile with a "You"
  self-view chip and a people-count chip, and a bottom icon toolbar.
- Move the always-on Performance HUD, raw feature dump, and benchmark
  panel behind toolbar toggle buttons (off by default) instead of
  showing FPS/perf numbers permanently — cleaner default view, still
  one click away.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MU45nrPCTAbLHpegrnUTs7
